    "notes": [
      {
        "moduleIds": [
          2
        ],
        "content": "## Generate proposals from HubSpot deals with Claude in Google Docs\n\nSales and operations teams that assemble proposals and statements of work from the last one, every time.\n\n### How it works\nTrigger: A 'new proposal' form, a deal moving to the proposal stage in the CRM, or an RFP document uploaded to a folder starts the run.\n1. Receive the request\n2. Pull the client record\n3. Parse the RFP or brief\n4. Retrieve past answers and case material\n5. Draft each section\n6. Consistency and compliance check\n7. Produce the document\n8. Route for review and learn\nEvery AI step is followed by a \"Needs a person?\" gate that parks low-confidence items; the write-back waits for an approval.\n\n### Setup\n1. Open \"Config (edit me)\" and fill in the fields (names, approver, quiet hours, thresholds).\n2. Add credentials: Anthropic, plus Pinecone / Supabase, Google Docs / Microsoft Word, HubSpot / Salesforce.\n3. Run once with test_mode on, read the output, then switch the trigger on.\n\n### Customization tips\nStore your section templates in the Config node; swap Google Docs for Microsoft Word and HubSpot for Salesforce.\nGuardrail to keep: Every reused answer is sourced to the document it came from; the writer can see what was adapted.\n\nFull blueprint: https://agentmelt.com/workflows/document-generation-automation/",
        "isFilterNote": false,
        "metadata": {
          "color": "#F5D451"
        }
      }
    ],
    "zone": "eu1.make.com"
  }
}